Track 1: Pendulums Chew the Salt
- Story & Context: At the crossroads bazaar of Bir Qattar, elder salvage scout Othman cracked open the chassis of a buried 1988 Yamaha DX7 only to find its internal clock chips rusted into green slag. As his butane torch hissed against melted copper and scorched wolf-fur insulation, an unexpected electrical ground loop caused the caravan's solar-powered master timers to tick backwards at double-time. Vespera plugged straight into the sparking inverter, unleashing hyper-velocity thrash riffs over a rolling 128 BPM tech-house kick while Malik's tenor sax howled through the dust storm like a ruptured locomotive horn. Standing over the smoking console as panic swept the market stalls, Othman raised his blackened pliers and bellowed: "The dial broke when the iron began to scream!"
