Track 2: "You Were Supposed to Ring at Equinox"
- Story & Context: Deep in the corrugated cargo bay of Rig Four, sound engineer Leyla scraped baked salt crust from the voice cards of a scavenged Roland Juno-106 while sobbing motor oil onto her leather apron. She had broken caravan law by lingering three weeks at the dry well of Erg Chebbi to scavenge an elusive analog filter board, entirely missing the seasonal equinox rendezvous that supplied water to her brother’s convoy. The track captures her spiraling guilt through a mournful, fuzz-soaked tenor saxophone solo that wrestles against a punishing, pneumatic tech-house bass groove and double-kick gallops that sound like an engine throwing a piston. Gripping a distorted communication microphone with scarred fingers, Leyla screamed her confession across the dead airwaves: "I counted seven sunsets against the rusted hull, but nobody answered my bell."
